/S /P
/E (Unlike traditional presentations, films opened space for participants to feel the issues before analyzing them. Through stories of housing struggles, community resilience, and everyday negotiations with city systems, participants were drawn into conversations that bridged policy, research, and lived experience.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
